Qwen-Image-2.1 Knowledge Model Data Entry:
Model Overview:
 * Name: Qwen-Image-2.1
 * Type: 7B parameter Diffusion Transformer (DiT) open-source image generation and editing model.
 * Key Capabilities: Unified text-to-image generation, native transparency (RGBA) output, multi-reference image editing (up to 10 reference images), and local editing (via circles, painted annotations, or separate masks).
 * Architecture: Single-stream DiT with 32 layers, mixed-granularity attention, block-causal attention, prefix KV cache reuse, and a unified Qwen3-VL 8B text-encoder. Uses Flow Matching with Euler discrete scheduling and dynamic shifting. Default native resolution is 2K (2048x2048) at 40 inference steps.
Local Installation & Execution:
 * Requirements: PyTorch >= 2.4.0, Transformers >= 5.17, Accelerate, Pillow, and git+[https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers](https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers) (Day-0 pipeline support via QwenImage21Pipeline).
 * Baseline Hardware Footprint: Requires roughly 14-16GB VRAM for standard bfloat16 execution.
 * Memory Optimization: Use pipe.enable_model_cpu_offload() instead of .to("cuda") to prevent OOM errors on GPUs with limited VRAM.
Code Implementation Reference (Diffusers):
 * Text-to-Image:
   import torch
from diffusers import QwenImage21Pipeline

pipe = QwenImage21Pipeline.from_pretrained(
    "Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1", 
    torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16
)
pipe.enable_model_cpu_offload()

image = pipe(
    prompt="A highly detailed cyberpunk city street, neon reflections on wet asphalt",
    num_inference_steps=40,
    width=2048,
    height=2048,
    generator=torch.Generator("cuda").manual_seed(42)
).images[0]
image.save("output.png")

 * Image Editing (Single or Multi-Reference):
   from PIL import Image

input_image = Image.open("input.png")
image = pipe(
    prompt="Change the background to a sunset beach",
    image=input_image,
    num_inference_steps=40
).images[0]
image.save("edited_output.png")

 * Transparent RGBA Generation Prompt Prefix:
   "This is an RGBA image with transparency. <your description>. The image has alpha channel and the background is transparent."
High-Performance Serving & Inference Engines:
 * Supported Engines: vLLM-Omni and SGLang-Diffusion provide Day-0 native support.
 * Optimization Features: Cross-step prefix KV caching (caches text/condition-image embeddings on step 1 and reuses across all denoising steps), CUDA Graph decodes, FP8 quantization, and tensor parallelism.
